    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_ede9284f",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Mysogynous; overall-intent-description: The meme juxtaposes a sloth (often used as a humorous, slow-moving animal) with a woman's face, using the text 'do you like to barbeque cause i'm bout to slap this meat across your grill.' The phrase 'slap this meat' is a crude, sexually suggestive metaphor that objectifies the woman by reducing her to a piece of meat, which is a misogynistic trope. The visual of the woman's face, combined with the vulgar text, is intended to be provocative and degrading, targeting women through objectification and sexualization. This aligns with misogynous content as it uses the woman's body as a target for ridicule and degradation, fitting the 'objectification/body part focus' and 'sexual availability assumptions' categories under misogyny.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_4cc7d820"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
